{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f7e6388a-d4e4-5f7e-ae46-bb40c3a65d1b",
    "name": "Products API",
    "description": "Colección ejecutable de la Products API.\n\n**Uso manual:** ejecuta primero `1. Auth → Login (admin)` (guarda el token). Las variables ya apuntan a los datos demo (`productId` = 1, Laptop Pro 14; `usdId`/`eurId`/`mxnId` = 1/2/3), así que cualquier request funciona en cualquier orden.\n\n**Uso completo:** *Run collection* ejecuta las carpetas en orden; cada request guarda lo que necesita el siguiente (crea su propio producto y al final lo elimina y revoca el token). Desde terminal: `make e2e`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "viewerToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "usdId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "eurId",
      "value": "2"
    },
    {
      "key": "mxnId",
      "value": "3"
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Obtén un token Bearer. El login de admin guarda `{{token}}`; el de viewer, `{{viewerToken}}`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Credenciales demo de administrador. Guarda el token en `{{token}}`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password\",\n  \"device_name\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test(\"Bearer with read+write\", () => { pm.expect(d.token_type).to.eql(\"Bearer\"); pm.expect(d.abilities).to.eql([\"products:read\",\"products:write\"]); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", d.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (viewer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"viewer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password\",\n  \"device_name\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test(\"Read-only abilities\", () => pm.expect(d.abilities).to.eql([\"products:read\"]));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"viewerToken\", d.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
